# Cinematic Video Player Redesign

The user wants a more "video-like" experience, similar to a React component that features a progress slider, transport controls, and cinematic title transitions. I will pivot the "Presentation Mode" to be a dedicated **Cinematic Player**.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **UI Transition**: The "Sidebar Editorial" layout will be moved to a secondary "Document View". The default **Presentation Mode** will now be a **Holographic Video Player** with:
> - **Floating Glassmorphism Overlays**: Narration and Equations will float in the top-left, rather than being in a sidebar.
> - **Transport Controls**: A centered bottom bar with Play/Pause, Skip, and a **Progress Slider**.
> - **Impactful Titles**: The opening of a lesson will feature a large, centered title that fades and moves to the top-left, exactly like the user's example.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name] Styling & Logic

#### [MODIFY] [style.css](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/MathViz/src/style.css)
- Add styles for `.cinematic-overlay` (glassmorpism).
- Add styles for `.video-player-bar` (floating controls).
- Add styles for `.cinematic-title` (animatable large title).
- Ensure `.pres-container` supports many layers (Viz -> Title -> Overlays -> Controls).

#### [MODIFY] [app.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/MathViz/src/app.ts)
- **Refactor `renderPresentation`**:
  - Create a `#presentation-root` that occupies the whole area.
  - Layer 1: `#pres-viz` (Manim Canvas).
  - Layer 2: `#pres-title-overlay` (Large opening title).
  - Layer 3: `#pres-narrative-overlay` (Floating Card for narration/math).
  - Layer 4: `#pres-player-bar` (Progress slider + Buttons).
- **Update `updatePresentationState`**:
  - Handle the **Step 0 Title Logic**: If index is 0, show the title large/centered. If index > 0, move it to the corner or hide it.
- **Implement Progress Slider**: Replace the dots with a `<input type="range">` that syncs with `currentBeatIndex`.

#### [MODIFY] [Gram-Schmidt Lesson Data]
- Add an opening "Title Beat" (Step 0) with no math/narration, just the title.
- Align the narrative steps to the user's provided timeline.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- `npm run build` to ensure no regression.

### Manual Verification
- Open `http://localhost:5175/` and enter Presentation Mode.
- Verify the **Play/Pause** flow.
- Ensure the **Progress Slider** correctly jumps to beats.
- Verify the **Floating Math Card** doesn't block the visual center.
